cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Machine Learning on AWS with SageMaker and Bedrock
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
authors:
  - given-names: Christopher
    family-names: Endemann
    email: endemann@wisc.edu
    affiliation: University of Wisconsin-Madison
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7357-6129'
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/carpentries-incubator/ML_with_AWS_SageMaker
url: >-
  https://carpentries-incubator.github.io/ML_with_AWS_SageMaker/index.html
abstract: >-
  This hands-on workshop teaches researchers how to run
  machine learning and AI workloads on AWS, from preparing
  data in S3 to training models, fine-tuning, and running
  inference. Participants use SageMaker to train XGBoost and
  PyTorch models, tune hyperparameters, and fine-tune a
  vision-language model for historical handwriting
  recognition. They also build retrieval-augmented
  generation (RAG) pipelines over research papers, comparing
  hosted models on Amazon Bedrock with open-weight models
  running on SageMaker GPUs. Throughout the exercises,
  participants learn how to choose compute resources,
  estimate costs before running jobs, track actual usage,
  and clean up resources afterward. The workshop assumes
  basic Python and machine learning experience but no prior
  knowledge of AWS.
